{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/237528-seeming-contracts","id":237528,"title":"Seeming Contracts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-22T17:13:59-07:00","id":237528,"title":"Seeming Contracts","content":"I was wondering what exactly qualifies as a Seeming Contract... at least in regard to meeting the two dot minimum for character creation. Does this mean any contract that a Changeling of a given Seeming has affinity for... or just the ones specifically referred to as such from the Core and Winter Masques. There were some contracts present in a few other books that only some Seemings have affinity for (such as Contract of the Wild from Rites of Spring)... would these also be considered Seeming Contracts? I'm leaning towards the ides that only the contracts that a given Seeming has affinity for would qualify... if every Seeming can access it easily, then it doesn't qualify.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T18:14:34-07:00","id":237591,"title":"","content":"Beasts-Fang and Talon, Den, Wyld<br /> Elementals-Elements, Communion, Wyld<br /> Darklings-Darkness, Spirits and Shades<br /> Fairest-Vainglory, Separation, Reflection<br /> Ogre-Strength, Oath and Punishment<br /> Wizened-Artifice, Animation, Forge","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T06:32:11-07:00","id":238130,"title":"","content":"The intended reading is <i>probably</i> the same as yours.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T22:41:44-07:00","id":238869,"title":"","content":"Yeah... I figured that contracts that specified they were affinity for specific Seemings were considered &quot;Seeming Contracts&quot; for the purpose of the 2 dot minimum while contracts that were affinity for all Changelings belonged in the General category and didn't count. Just wanted to make sure I was reading things right.<br /> <br /> A few people I play with (on both sides of the ST screen) have tried to make the argument that any contract a Changeling has an affinity for qualifies as a &quot;Seeming&quot; contract since they come just as easily as their &quot;Seeming&quot; contracts do.<br /> <br /> In a way, this does make a certain amount of sense because these additional contracts <u>do</u> come naturally to Changelings... just as naturally as their &quot;Seeming&quot; contracts do. I could see an <i>Oracle</i> focusing exclusively on the Contract of Omens, a <i>Witchtooth </i>on the Contract of Hearth or a <i>Moonborn </i>focusing on the Contract of the Moon. In fact... some of the &quot;Seeming&quot; Contracts just might not fit with the way player wants to portray a given Changeling. Perhaps they have a <i>Mirrorskin </i>who's player feels that neither the Contracts of Darkness nor Spirits and Shades really fits the concept he is going for (Master Shapshifter/Spy) but the Contract of Mirror does... and since it comes as easily to this changeling as the other two contracts would (and makes a better fit for a Changeling who's nature is to mimic others), it would make some sense, yes?<br /> <br /> Given the sometimes limited options the official &quot;Seeming&quot; contracts give... opening up the others would allow a greater diversity of possible powers amongst Changelings. True... many will still lean towards the standard contracts... but there is always an exception to the rules... especially where Changelings are involved.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":2243,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","user":"Shadowstripe","date":". 08-24-2014, 06:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T18:13:05-07:00","id":242718,"title":"","content":"My personal experience has always been that the two-dot affinity rule applies to contracts that are either a) General Affinity Contracts (Eg, Dream, Hearth, Omen) or b) Seeming Affinity Contracts (Eg, Fang&amp;Talon for Beasts) and that it was only meant to restrict a Changeling for example taking 4 Dots of Oath And Punishment as an Elemental at creation.<br /> <br /> For what it's worth, the mechanical implementation in Hero Lab rule-checks it in this way as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}